      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "I2C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) is a two-wire serial protocol for connecting low-speed peripherals (sensors, EEPROMs, touch controllers) to a microprocessor.",
      "source_hash": 9338760474806372563,
      "context_hash": 15588236053925693008,
      "translation": "I2C(Inter-Integrated Circuit)는 저속 주변 장치(센서, EEPROM, 터치 컨트롤러)를 마이크로프로세서에 연결하기 위한 2선식 직렬 프로토콜입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "controller": "컨트롤러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:53:15.144682Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "The Linux I2C subsystem was carried into the mainline kernel through Greg Kroah-Hartman's driver-model work and later co-maintained by Jean Delvare (formerly of the lm-sensors project), who took sole maintainership in September 2005 [(LWN: I2C patches for 2.6.12-rc1)](https://lwn.net/Articles/130158/).",
      "source_hash": 14778106485510188208,
      "context_hash": 11990280102074296878,
      "translation": "Linux I2C 서브시스템은 Greg Kroah-Hartman의 드라이버 모델 작업을 통해 메인라인 커널에 들어왔으며, 이후 Jean Delvare(전 lm-sensors 프로젝트 소속)가 공동으로 유지보수하다가 2005년 9월에 단독 메인테이너가 되었습니다 [(LWN: I2C patches for 2.6.12-rc1)](https://lwn.net/Articles/130158/).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "LWN": "LWN",
        "Linux": "Linux",
        "mainline": "메인라인",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:25:33.874719Z",
      "issues": []
